Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-12-2001||02:20 PM||||Grassroots motorsports did a comparison of a bunch of miata's a while back. In the field there were a few Supercharged cars..<P>mid 7 sec to sixty ...mid to low 15's in the 1/4<P>Giddy Up.<P>There is a guy that comes out to our local strip with a turbo miata , 1.8 later car with no IC , runs 15.4's<P>Again ...Giddy up....do you detect the sarcasm??<P>As for handling... Miatas are hard to beat , they just need more power.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||09-12-2001||02:53 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.monstermotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.monstermotorsports.com/</A> <P>Giddy that up.<P>-Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||09-12-2001||04:05 PM||||I have seen monster miatas before at autocrosses. <P>Nothing like taking a well balanced car and putting a boat anchor for a motor in it.<P>Snow plow anyone?? The car understeered all over the place even with a setup suspension and was the squirliest car I have ever seen. The stock 1.6 early miatas were whooping it bad.<P><BR>Keep your monster boat anchor. You can stuff a V8 in anything you want , doesn't mean it's a good combo. (Fiero's excluded)<P>JM  <BR>||||reg||1
