Z||000007||artherd||09-13-2001||02:39 AM||||I know of a man who has a Rover V8 Miata.  (keep in mind, this is an all-aluminum, OHV &lt;far lighter, if not more powerful, heads&gt; 3500cc v8 engine.)<P>Yeah, cute little 3.5l V8.  His weight bias is about 55/45 or so he says.<P>Never seen the car in person, but that's probally what I would do to any miata I owned  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(and I'd only own the '95 Merlot M eddition, those are sweet cars!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||Carrolles||09-13-2001||08:01 AM||||My friend borrowed my G-Tech Pro to do before and after readings of the Supercharged Miata.  His clutch slips badly with the new power so the readings aren't very impressive so far.  The stock pressure plate has around 1200 pounds clamping force.  Tests have shown stock pressure plates with as little as 900 pounds clamping force.<P>He is installing a Star Performance clutch with a 1700 pound pressure plate this week.  It will be interesting to see what it'll do.<P>The stock Miata has no guts in the low end.  He has to launch at high rpm's to force the tires to break loose so he doesn't stall.  Trap speeds are pretty good though.<P>I wasn't suggesting that a supercharged Miata is the best thing since sliced bread I was simply implying that if it did that much good on the Miata 1.8 think what it would do to a built 3.4 Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||09-13-2001||01:42 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.enthuzacar.com" TARGET=_blank>www.enthuzacar.com</A>  thats the new owner of Engineered Performance.. he's got a 280hp turbo miata...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  anyone close to atl i'll gladly take for a slide. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.avoturbo.com" TARGET=_blank>www.avoturbo.com</A>  the turbo kit he used... and David Wallens (senior editor of GRM) has a n/a car make 145hp at the wheels(help build that car).. that a fun car and it's quiet.. no rotors to whine..  you can't help but fall in love with the whine under boost!  <P>you can get rebuilt M90s for about $700 that'll support the 2.8 with PLENTY of room to spare. ||||reg||1
